      evolution: 'From Medieval Latin "supervidere," combining "super" (over, above) and "videre" (to see). The imagery is powerful: a supervisor "sees over" the work, watching from an elevated position. It entered English in the 15th century. The Latin "videre" is one of the most productive roots in English, giving us "vision," "video," "evidence," "provide," "revise," "visible," and many more. The concept of oversight from above connects to the hierarchical nature of management.',
